# Data Catalog for Gold Layer

## Overview

The Gold Layer represents the business-level data mart for the Healthcare Data Warehouse system. It is structured into **Dimension Views** and **Fact Views** using a **Star Schema** to support analytical reporting and BI dashboards (e.g., Power BI).

---

### 1. **gold.dim_patients**

* **Purpose:** Stores comprehensive demographic, contact, and insurance information for patients.
* **Columns:**

| Column Name | Data Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| patient_key | INT | Surrogate key uniquely identifying each patient record in the dimension table. |
| patient_id | VARCHAR(50) | Natural business key assigned to the patient from the source system. |
| first_name | VARCHAR(50) | The patient's first name. |
| last_name | VARCHAR(50) | The patient's last or family name. |
| full_name | VARCHAR(100) | Concatenated full name of the patient (e.g., 'John Doe'). |
| gender | VARCHAR(20) | Standardized gender of the patient (e.g., 'Male', 'Female'). |
| date_of_birth | DATE | Date of birth of the patient (YYYY-MM-DD). |
| contact_number | VARCHAR(50) | Phone contact number of the patient. |
| address | VARCHAR(255) | Residential address of the patient. |
| registration_date | DATE | Date when the patient registered with the hospital system. |
| insurance_provider | VARCHAR(100) | Name of the insurance provider company (e.g., 'MedCare Plus'). |
| insurance_number | VARCHAR(50) | Unique policy or insurance identification number. |
| email | VARCHAR(100) | Cleaned and lowercased email address of the patient. |

---

### 2. **gold.dim_doctors**

* **Purpose:** Holds master profiles of physicians, including specialization and hospital branch assignments.
* **Columns:**

| Column Name | Data Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| doctor_key | INT | Surrogate key uniquely identifying each doctor in the dimension table. |
| doctor_id | VARCHAR(50) | Natural business key assigned to the doctor. |
| first_name | VARCHAR(50) | The doctor's first name. |
| last_name | VARCHAR(50) | The doctor's last name. |
| full_name | VARCHAR(100) | Formatted full name with title (e.g., 'Dr. Sarah Connor'). |
| specialization | VARCHAR(50) | Medical field of expertise (e.g., 'Pediatrics', 'Oncology', 'Dermatology'). |
| phone_number | VARCHAR(50) | Work contact number for the doctor. |
| years_experience | INT | Total years of professional medical practice. |
| hospital_branch | VARCHAR(100) | Assigned hospital branch location (e.g., 'Central Hospital', 'Westside Clinic'). |
| email | VARCHAR(100) | Professional email address of the doctor. |

---

### 3. **gold.fact_appointment**

* **Purpose:** Captures operational healthcare transactions, appointment attendance statuses, and clinical procedures performed.
* **Columns:**

| Column Name | Data Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| appointment_key | INT | Primary surrogate key for each appointment fact line item. |
| appointment_id | VARCHAR(50) | Natural key identifying the specific appointment transaction. |
| doctor_key | INT | Foreign key linking the appointment to `gold.dim_doctors`. |
| patient_key | INT | Foreign key linking the appointment to `gold.dim_patients`. |
| treatment_id | VARCHAR(50) | Unique key for the medical treatment performed during the appointment (if any). |
| reason_for_visit | VARCHAR(100) | Primary medical reason for the visit (e.g., 'Checkup', 'Consultation', 'Emergency'). |
| treatment_type | VARCHAR(100) | Type of procedure or test performed (e.g., 'MRI', 'Chemotherapy', 'X-Ray'). |
| treatment_description | VARCHAR(255) | Detailed description of the clinical treatment administered. |
| status | VARCHAR(50) | Operational status of the appointment (e.g., 'Completed', 'No-show', 'Cancelled'). |
| treatment_cost | DECIMAL(10,2) | Cost incurred for the medical procedure/treatment performed. |
| appointment_date | DATE | Date when the appointment took place or was scheduled for. |
| appointment_time | TIME(0) | Exact time of the appointment, formatted without fractional seconds. |
| treatment_date | DATE | Specific date when the treatment was executed. |

---

### 4. **gold.fact_billing**

* **Purpose:** Tracks financial metrics, billing totals, payment statuses, and revenue channels.
* **Columns:**

| Column Name | Data Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| bill_key | INT | Primary surrogate key for each financial billing transaction record. |
| bill_id | VARCHAR(50) | Unique invoice/bill identifier. |
| patient_key | INT | Foreign key linking the financial bill to `gold.dim_patients`. |
| treatment_id | VARCHAR(50) | Identifier of the medical treatment associated with this bill. |
| payment_method | VARCHAR(50) | Payment channel used by the patient (e.g., 'Credit Card', 'Insurance', 'Cash'). |
| payment_status | VARCHAR(50) | Status of financial collection (e.g., 'Paid', 'Pending', 'Failed'). |
| amount | DECIMAL(10,2) | Total billed monetary value for the medical service. |
| bill_date | DATE | Date when the invoice/bill was generated. |
